WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.061
Week 28: Subjunctive: Doubt, Purpose, and Contingency. qualify certainty state purpose and conditions plan for contingencies

2
00:00:09.061 --> 00:00:16.521
Mission brief. Assess an uncertain report and propose a plan with purpose, deadline, and fallback conditions.

3
00:00:16.521 --> 00:00:25.926
Preparation. Select ten useful words, three linking expressions, and two repair phrases. Plan points rather than a memorized paragraph.

4
00:00:25.926 --> 00:00:33.707
Performance. Complete the task once for fluency, review the evidence, then repeat it for greater clarity and accuracy.

5
00:00:33.707 --> 00:00:42.234
After-action review. Record what succeeded, what blocked communication, and the single change that will matter most on the next attempt.

6
00:00:42.234 --> 00:01:14.039
Model language. Voy a evaluar un informe incierto. — I am going to evaluate an uncertain report. Propongo un plan con un propósito claro. — I propose a plan with a clear purpose. Incluyo una fecha límite realista. — I include a realistic deadline. Preparo una alternativa por si acaso. — I prepare an alternative just in case. Tengo un plan de contingencia salvo que todo salga bien. — I have a contingency plan unless everything goes well.

7
00:01:14.039 --> 00:01:23.937
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
